## 2. AI Media Content Creation → Instagram Auto-Post

**Idea:** Give it a word or theme, it generates an image and caption using AI, and posts it to Instagram automatically (or as a scheduled/reviewed post).

**Architecture Split by Language**
| Language | Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| **Python** | Entire pipeline | Caption generation (LLM API) → image generation (Stable Diffusion/DALL·E API) → posting (Instagram Graph API) → scheduling (APScheduler) |

This one is intentionally single-language — the whole pipeline is a sequence of API calls and light orchestration, which doesn't benefit from splitting across languages the way a high-concurrency system would.

**Roadmap**
| Phase | Task | Language | Tech Stack |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Set up Instagram Business account + Graph API access (dev mode) | — | Meta for Developers |
| 1 | Build caption generation from a theme/word | Python | LLM API |
| 2 | Build image generation from the same theme | Python | Stable Diffusion API / DALL·E API |
| 3 | Build the Instagram publish flow (upload media container → publish) | Python | Instagram Graph API, `requests` |
| 4 | Add a review/approval step before auto-posting | Python | Simple CLI prompt or small Flask review UI |
| 5 | Add scheduling (post at a set time) | Python | APScheduler / cron |
| 6 | Add logging of what was generated/posted, for review later | Python | SQLite |
| 7 | Deploy as a scheduled script on a small server | Python | Docker, cron job |

