# POLYGLOT-BY-NECESSITY PROJECT

## 12. Smart Electricity Monitoring System (+ Auto Power-Off for TV/AC)

**Idea:** Sensors on individual sockets track how long and how much current each appliance draws, feeding a dashboard that shows which appliances waste power — extended with automatic power cutoff for devices (TV, AC) left idle for too long, to reduce the electricity bill.

**Architecture Split by Language**
| Language | Component | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| **Rust (or C/C++)** | Sensor Firmware | Runs on the microcontroller (ESP32), reads current draw per socket, publishes readings via MQTT, triggers a relay to cut power when idle-threshold is crossed |
| **Go** | Ingestion Backend | Consumes MQTT messages from many sockets concurrently, writes to a time-series database, decides (and sends) the idle-cutoff command back to the firmware |
| **Python** | Analytics | Runs pattern analysis over stored data — "this appliance is wasteful," idle-time detection, daily/weekly usage reports |

**Roadmap**
| Phase | Task | Language | Tech Stack |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | Scope hardware: which sockets, which sensor (current clamp/INA219), which microcontroller (ESP32) | — | Hardware planning |
| 1 | Build firmware to read current draw and publish over MQTT | Rust (`esp-rs`) or C++ | ESP32, MQTT (Mosquitto broker) |
| 2 | Build the Go ingestion service consuming MQTT messages | Go | `paho.mqtt.golang`, TimescaleDB/InfluxDB |
| 3 | Store readings in a time-series database | Go | TimescaleDB or InfluxDB |
| 4 | Build the idle-detection logic (near-zero draw for N minutes → flag) | Go | Plain logic |
| 5 | Add the relay cutoff command sent back to firmware over MQTT | Go + Rust/C++ | MQTT (bidirectional topic) |
| 6 | Build Python analytics: per-appliance usage patterns, wasteful-device flagging | Python | Pandas, scheduled job |
| 7 | Build the dashboard | Grafana or Python (Streamlit) | Grafana / Streamlit |
| 8 | Test the full loop: sensor reading → cutoff decision → relay trigger | Go + Rust/C++ | Manual hardware test |
| 9 | Document the full pipeline (sensor → broker → backend → analytics → dashboard) | — | README with architecture diagram |

